# Line endings and byte-exact files (friction register FR-C-022).
#
# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, whatever the contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Windows tools
# (Python's csv module, PowerShell 5.1, many editors) write CRLF by default, and mixed endings make diffs noisy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF to run.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Game text formats keep their bytes exactly: round-trip goldens compare them byte for byte, and the formats use CRLF
# and tabs by convention (mission.sqm, scripts, description.ext and its includes). Git must never rewrite them.
*.sqm -text
*.sqs -text
*.sqf -text
*.ext -text
*.hpp -text
*.cpp -text
*.h -text
*.fsm -text
# A mission's string table; this repository's own CSV files stay LF text.
stringtable.csv -text

# Binary game, model and image formats.
*.pbo binary
*.paa binary
*.pac binary
*.p3d binary
*.wrp binary
*.wss binary
*.ogg binary
*.bin binary
*.gguf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
